      },
      "worked": "Compare the prices for the same mass.\n$$\\begin{align*}1\\text{ kg }50\\text{ g}&=1050\\text{ g}\\\\\\text{Cost of 1 g at the smaller option's rate}&=\\frac{\\$4.50}{250}=\\$0.018\\\\\\text{Cost of 1050 g at the smaller option's rate}&=\\$0.018\\times1050=\\$18.90\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\$12<\\$18.90$, the 1 kg 50 g option is more economical.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
